/-! # Degree-`4` first-integral `ν` bridge for the normalized `(8,10)` nonzero source

On the nonzero first face `H = h²`, `N = 5 p₇ H - 4 q₉ = λ h⁹` with
`h.natDegree = 1`, the degree-`5` first integral `μ` is cleared and
jet-peeled by the imported terminal integral bridge; the genuinely
unused degree-`4` first integral `ν` of the same source differential
system is the next isolated mechanism.  Its exact construction
(`nuResidual810`, linear in the degree-`8` row residual `θ`), its
`d ν = 0` law on the depressed rows of degree `8`, `7`, `6`, and `4`,
its weight-`91` polynomial numerator
(`localClearedThirteenthDefect810 = 281474976710656 h⁹¹ ν`), and its
scale-two literal-source power relation
(`nonzeroFace810_thirteenthDefectPowerRelation`, cleared defect
`C nuGround * h₀⁹¹`) are all reused opaquely from the imported
scale-zero twelfth-defect scratch — the weight-`84` `μ` numerator and
the weight-`91` `ν` numerator are never re-expanded here.

This file adds the scale-two jet peel and the branch combination.  The
seventeenth-face jet `p₇ = h₀⁶ t₀`, `p₆ = h₀⁴ v₁`, `p₅ = h₀² u₁`,
`q₈ = h₀⁶ s₁`, `q₇ = h₀⁴ w₁`, `q₆ = h₀² b₆₂` factors the `ν` numerator
through `h₀⁷⁸`, thirteen orders below the defect weight — one order
deeper than the twelve-order `μ` peel: the peeled power relation is
`head + h₀ · tail = C nuGround · h₀¹³`, so the order-`78` head
vanishes at the root of `h₀` on every live branch.  The head is a
`121`-term polynomial in the same eight jet coordinates as the `μ`
head, with every monomial of jet degree at least three.

On the left branch the head reduces, modulo the second/third-defect
reductions, the `Gred`/`Vred` loads, and exact division by the `μ`
left residual (quotient `-64 t₀`), to a new exact degree-`13` relation
on `(t₀, v₁, u₁, b₆₂)` alone (`bridgeNuLeftResidual810`); it is not in
the ideal generated by the reduced fourth- through seventh-defect
loads and the `μ` left residual, on either `F₁` or `F₂`, so it is
genuinely new and neither left sub-branch closes.

On the collapsed right branch every jet coordinate is a multiple of
`h₀`, the substituted head and tail acquire three further `h₀` orders,
and the quotient peel collapses to the single monomial
`-54975581388800 a₄₁² b₅₁`: at the root
`(p₄/h₀)(a)² · (q₅/h₀)(a) = 0`, giving the strictly deeper divisibility
alternative `h₀² ∣ p₄ ∨ h₀² ∣ q₅` on both right sub-branches — the
first refinement past the `μ` collapse.  The inhomogeneous Keller
boundary relation `G'(a) W(a) - F(a) X'(a) = j ≠ 0` lives on
`p₀, p₁, q₀, q₁`, which neither new consequence touches, so no branch
is genuinely inconsistent and none is closed.

The `μ` ground constant `eta`, the new `ν` ground constant
`nuGround`, the tracked ground constants `δ, ε, ζ, η`, the aligned
face `N = 0`, both `μ` children (the left `F₁ ∨ F₂` alternative with
all retained next-order laws and the right sibling/complementary
sub-branches with their witness laws), and every previously recorded
residual are preserved and restated.  The next unused first integral
on this face is the degree-`3` integral `ξ`
(`xiResidual810`, weight-`98`).

No total-degree or twice-prime theorem is used.
-/

